"""Turning two sets of measurements into a defensible statement.

Pure functions only. The hard part is not arithmetic, it is refusing to call noise an improvement: this machine is a
fanless MacBook Air, and its run-to-run drift is routinely larger than the optimisations being measured. So:

  noise floor    per side, (max - min) / median over that side's repeats
  threshold      max(the louder side's noise floor, MIN_RELATIVE_CHANGE)
  BETTER/WORSE   only when the median moved further than the threshold, in the metric's own good direction

Correctness is handled by gates, not by thresholds. A gate failure makes the whole record BROKEN whatever the
latency did, because a faster engine that decides differently has not been optimised, it has been changed.
